# Test sources are never compiled into the image: every package/app tsconfig
# builds `src/**` only and excludes `**/*.test.ts`, so nothing under these paths
# can reach `/out`. Excluding them keeps a test-only edit from invalidating the
# `COPY . .` layer and forcing a full ~8-minute rebuild — which is exactly what
# blows the 300s `beforeAll` hook timeout in
# packages/router/test/containers-real-docker.e2e.test.ts (that suite builds this
# image itself). Recorded as a gotcha by the 2026-07-17 router-mode drive.
packages/*/test
apps/*/test
**/*.test.ts

# ---- Deployment parameter files: LOAD-BEARING FOR SECRECY -------------------
# Do not prune these as "unused" or "just build speed". scripts/deploy-router-image.sh
# runs `az acr build … .`, which tars the whole working directory and UPLOADS it
# to the registry, honouring this file (azure-cli
# command_modules/acr/_archive_utils.py: _pack_source_code -> _load_dockerignore_file).
# Without these entries every deploy would ship, off this machine:
#   infra/azure/bicep/main.bicepparam   mode 600 — may temporarily hold bootstrap/rotation secrets
# It is not needed by docker/router/Dockerfile, which builds only the pnpm
# workspace — pnpm-workspace.yaml is `packages/*` + `apps/*`, so infra/ is not a member.
#
# The Terraform state and provider-cache rules that used to live here are gone
# with the Terraform stack: the deployment is Bicep and holds no state locally.
# A populated bootstrap/rotation parameter file is the one remaining plaintext
# credential bundle on disk; the steady-state file is intentionally secretless.
#
# Both the bare and the `**/` form of each rule are required. ACR compiles
# `**/x` to `^.*/x$` (needs at least one separator, so it misses a root-level
# file), `*.x` to `^[^/]*\.x$` (misses a nested one), and a trailing `/` to a
# pattern ending in `/$`, which no archive entry can ever match. Verified
# against the installed _archive_utils.IgnoreRule, not assumed.
#
# NOTE the ordering requirement: ACR (like Docker) applies the LAST matching
# rule, so the `!…example` negations must come after the patterns they re-admit.
# The example checklist carries no credential and is committed, so shipping it is
# harmless — it is un-ignored only to keep this file's semantics identical to
# .gitignore's, so one reading covers both.
*.bicepparam
**/*.bicepparam
!*.bicepparam.example
!**/*.bicepparam.example
# Residue of a SIGKILL'd rewrite in scripts/deploy-router-image.sh — a mode-600
# copy of main.bicepparam, so it must never be uploaded either.
*.bicepparam.tmp.*
**/*.bicepparam.tmp.*
# Compiled ARM output from `bicep build` — a build artifact, not a source.
infra/azure/bicep/**/*.json
